'''Transmembrane protease, serine 6''' (also known as matriptase-2) is an [[enzyme]] that in humans is encoded by the ''TMPRSS6'' [[gene]].<ref name="entrez">{{cite web | title = Entrez Gene: TMPRSS6 transmembrane protease, serine 6| url = https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/gene?Db=gene&Cmd=ShowDetailView&TermToSearch=164656| access-date = }}</ref>

Based on twin studies, mutations in TMPRSS6 gene have a correlation with iron deficiency predisposition.<ref>An P, Wu Q, Wang H, et al. TMPRSS6, but not TF, TFR2 or BMP2 variants are associated with increased risk of iron-deficiency anemia. Hum Mol Genet. 2012;21(9):2124-2131.</ref>

The protein encoded by this gene is a type II transmembrane serine proteinase that is found attached to the cell surface. The encoded protein may be involved in matrix remodeling processes in the liver.<ref name="entrez" />

